<title>GREECE: ASPIS BANK CUTS DEPO, LOAN RATES APRIL 15.</title>
<headline>ASPIS BANK CUTS DEPO, LOAN RATES APRIL 15.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aspis Bank said on Monday it is</p>
<p>cutting its deposit rates by 50 basis points along with</p>
<p>reductions in its mortgage and consumer loan rates, effective</p>
<p>April 15.</p>
<p>Aspis will offer the following rate structure:</p>
<p>DEPOSITS</p>
<p>    ** Savings deposit			9.5 - 10.0 percent</p>
<p>    ** Diamond savings account</p>
<p>	 up to 5.0 million drs		9.5</p>
<p>	 up to 30 million drs		10.75</p>
<p>	 over 30 million		     11.0</p>
<p>    ** Housing savings			9.5</p>
<p>CONSUMER LOANS</p>
<p>    ** Personal loan			 23.0  from 23.5 percent</p>
<p>MORTGAGES</p>
<p>    ** Floating rate mortgage	    15.75 from 16.0 percent</p>
<p>    ** Business housing loan	     15.75 from 16.25</p>
<p>    ** Fixed rate mortgage (3-year)    13.0  from 13.25</p>
<p>    ** Fixed rate mortgage (5-year)    11.9  (unchanged)</p>
<p>** Fixed rate business renovation  14.0  from 14.5</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-</p>
</text>
